            <ArticleTitle>The First Reported Case of Majocchi's Granuloma with Malbranchea sp. in an Immunocompetent Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9196528</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2017/9196528</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Majocchi's granuloma is a rare condition in which a dermatophyte invades the deeper layers of the dermis and subcutaneous tissue and can often be misidentified and treated as eczema. It has a variable presentation ranging from cutaneous lesions to deeper infections in immunocompromised patients. No prior cases have described the formation of Majocchi's granuloma with the deuteromycetes, Malabranchea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
